  "body": "Stacked on #3139 (merge #3139 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- The `expect` field of `case.toml` takes `\"post\"` or `\"refusal\"`. Other values are refused by name.\n- The 12 existing cases change to `expect = \"post\"`. #3139 held a free-text description there. The README of each case keeps that text.\n- A refusal case has no `<case>.nc`. It has `refusal.txt`: the refusal lines that the script host records, one line each.\n- The script of a refusal case saves the project, then runs the refused step without a catch. The script run ends with an error.\n- The app tests `regenerates` and `rebuilds` read `expect`:\n  - `regenerates` opens the saved project in the script host (`cam.load`, `cam.generate`, `cam.post`). It compares `ScriptOutcome::errors` with `refusal.txt`.\n  - `rebuilds` runs `build.camscript` with `camcraft-cli`. It requires a failed exit, a saved project, no `.nc`, and the same lines on stderr.\n  - The two tests also open the project and check that its model is embedded, with no file link.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check` accepts a refusal case without a `.nc` file. It runs the script and compares the refusal lines. A refusal case with a `.nc` file fails the layout check.\n- `cargo xtask catalog` (rebuild) writes `refusal.txt` for a refusal case.\n- New case `2d/drill-overfeed`: an 80 x 50 x 10 mm plate with two 6 mm holes. The Drill feeds at 400 mm/min, above the 115 mm/min of tool DR-0600. The post refuses it by the #2598 clause.\n- The 2D operation guide lists the new case under Drill (generated block).\n- The catalog README documents `expect` and `refusal.txt`.\n- The script host law does not change.\n\nProcess change: yes\nEffort: high. No escalation.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog tests and `--check` required a posted `.nc` for each case. A case could not show a refusal.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins:\n\n- `catalog_2d_drill_overfeed::regenerates`\n- `catalog_2d_drill_overfeed::rebuilds`\n- `catalog_check_verifies_refusal_case` (xtask integration)\n- `catalog_expect_takes_post_or_refusal_only`\n- `catalog_layout_accepts_a_refusal_case_without_nc`\n- `catalog_layout_still_requires_nc_for_a_post_case`\n- `refusal_lines_keep_the_cli_error_lines_without_the_prefix`\n- `a_changed_refusal_text_fails_the_check`\n\nMutation results (each red, then green after the restore):\n\n1. The app layout and dispatch as before (every case is a post case): the two case tests fail with `2d/drill-overfeed: missing drill-overfeed.nc`.\n2. `refusal.txt` says 120 mm/min in place of 115: the two case tests fail with `refusal lines differ from refusal.txt`. `cargo xtask catalog --check` fails with the want/got lines.\n3. The refusal case posts (feed lowered to 115 in the script and the project): `regenerates` fails with `the post was not refused`; `rebuilds` fails with `build.camscript ended without an error`.\n4. `xtask/src/catalog.rs` from #3139: `catalog_check_verifies_refusal_case` fails with `missing drill-overfeed.nc`.\n5. The `expect` value guard removed: `catalog_expect_takes_post_or_refusal_only` fails.\n6. The \"refusal case has a `.nc`\" guard removed: `catalog_layout_accepts_a_refusal_case_without_nc` fails.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: xtask unit tests ok. `app:example_catalog`: 33 passed, 2 failed.\n- The 2 failures are `catalog_2d_adaptive_pocket::regenerates` and `::rebuilds`: `did not finish within 60s`. The machine load average was 24-30.\n- The same two tests passed alone: 54.6 s and 55.2 s of the 60 s budget. This change touches only the `expect` line of that case. Follow-up #3163 reports the small margin.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --case 2d/drill-overfeed --check` passed.\n- `cargo test -p xtask catalog`: 23 unit tests and 6 integration tests passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets` (only the changed test target).\n- The full `cargo xtask catalog --check` over all cases (the seed case and the refusal case ran).\n- Screenshots and PDFs for the new case.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #3139: this PR changes the `expect` field that #3139 adds (`xtask/src/catalog_metadata.rs` `parse`, the 12 `case.toml` files and the tests that hold `expect` text). Merge #3139 first.\n- #3136 changes `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_2d_slots.rs` and the slots case files. This PR does not change them.\n\nChangelog: A catalog case can expect a refusal: `case.toml` `expect = \"refusal\"` compares the refusal lines with `refusal.txt`, and the new case 2d/drill-overfeed shows a refused post.\n\nFixes #2856\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
